  {:id       :verify-bridge-guest-cannot-execute
   :title    "the claude-bridge guest keeping the tools it is documented not to have"
   :why      "ADR-2608200200, 2026-08-20: the bridge's own header and the commit that
              shipped it both said a guest executing tools would be an agent running
              commands nobody sanctioned. The invariant was ASSERTED and never tested,
              and it was false -- `--allowedTools \"\"` is a PERMISSION allowlist, not an
              availability list, so all 25 built-ins stayed advertised and under
              permissionMode auto the guest ran Bash for real (`Run: echo
              hello-from-guest` -> tool_use Bash -> tool_result). The flag that removes
              availability is `--tools \"\"` (measured 25 -> 0). That fix landed and was
              checked by hand against a stub that was never committed, so nothing stops
              the next reader reaching the same wrong conclusion and deleting it. Static
              mode catches exactly that regression; --live is the only mode that proves
              the property, and it must probe with a value the model cannot produce
              without reading something -- the first attempt asked for `echo <marker>`,
              whose output is its own argument, and could not fail."
