  {:id       :verify-delegation-surfaces
   :title    "authority decided outside the lattice"
   :why      "ADR-2608180200, 2026-08-19: biscuit becomes the delegation centre and the
              decider stays ONE -- kotoba-lang/authority. authority.scope's docstring
              records what a second answer cost: covers? had been written once per URI
              scheme and one copy stripped a trailing * and called starts-with?, so
              kotoba://graph/alice* covered kotoba://graph/alice-evil. That copy is
              fixed and nothing checks for the next one. Wiring 130 repos by hand is not
              a plan; making the fleet able to answer where the decision is made is."
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" "{{repo}}:{{repo}}/scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-delegation-surfaces.cljs" "--check" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   ;; The floor pins the UNIT, not just a positive number. The old floor was
   ;; satisfied by "3,588 repos with a src/ tree" for months while the walk was
   ;; reading the wrong set -- a floor detects "measured nothing", never
   ;; "measured the wrong thing", so the unit has to be part of what it pins.
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\ttracked source file"
   :interval-ms 86400000                 ; 24h -- the shape changes slowly
   ;; Raised from 30m on 2026-08-21. The walk reads the INDEX, so git
   ;; decompresses blobs instead of the OS reading a checked-out tree -- that is
   ;; what correctness costs here, and the runtime is load-dependent. Re-measure
   ;; on a node rather than trusting the workstation number below.
   :timeout-ms  3600000                  ; 60m -- 3.6x a heavily-loaded measurement
   :writes   :none
   :measured "2026-08-21 on this machine: 16m43s wall at load average 100-200 (this
              workstation runs many parallel agents; a node will differ). SCANNED
              34,860 tracked source files across 3,661 of 4,211 on-disk repos, SKIPPED
              543 with no tracked source. 11 files in 5 repos hold both an authority
              string and a comparison; 3 of those repos fold into the lattice; the 3
              remaining findings are all test paths, reported at `info` and not failed
              on -- exit 0.

              The number that matters is not the zero, it is what the zero now means.
              The 2026-08-19 measurement recorded here read `3,588 repos with a src/
              tree, 1 file matched`, and was wrong in a way its own output could not
              show: the walk admitted a repo only if `<repo>/src` existed, which
              dropped 616 of 4,210 on-disk paths -- 132 of them holding Clojure source
              -- including `net-kotobase/control-plane`, the production edge API
              gateway of kotobase.net, whose `edge_chain.cljc` is titled `Delegation
              chains at the edge`. Its 6 matching files are visible now, and it folds
              into the lattice via `kotobase-api-gateway-cljs/deps.edn` -- which the
              old root-only `depends-on-authority?` would have missed, so a fixed walk
              alone would have produced 6 false findings. Blindness and misjudgement
              had cancelled into `clean`.

              `--self-test` now covers the WALK as well as the matchers: 6/6 matcher
              cases and 5/5 walk cases, the latter building a real git repository
              shaped like the hazard (source under a sub-project, one file tracked but
              deleted from the worktree, a nested deps.edn) and asserting the scan
              arrives. Proven in both directions on that fixture: the old walk answers
              `present? false` and `lattice? false`; the new one returns both files and
              `lattice? true`. See ADR-2608210300 -- the previous self-test proved the
              matchers discriminate 5/5 and proved nothing about the walk, and the walk
              was what was broken."}

