  {:id       :verify-valueflows-binding
   :title    "the cloud-itonami Valueflows projections, and the ISIC tables under them"
   :why      "ADR-2608153000, 2026-08-15: the binding that puts 1,398 cloud-itonami
              businesses on the Valueflows plane is a committed projection derived from
              blueprints plus the mirrored UN ISIC tables, and every input is outside
              the repo that holds it. Its first version reported 497 classified
              businesses of which up to 121 had the WRONG industry name, because it
              resolved Rev.5-declared codes against the only mirrored table, which was
              Rev.4 -- 83 of the 361 codes in both tables mean different things (1104 is
              soft drinks in Rev.4 and malt in Rev.5). Nothing would have caught that
              recurring. The Rev.4 half of the mirror is also unpinned and disputed
              against the UN legacy structure file on 33 of 414 titles, which 122
              businesses' industry names currently rest on; if that record and the mirror
              stop agreeing, a human has to decide which vintage is authoritative, and
              silently is the one way it must not happen. 2026-08-15 addition: the
              uchiwake resource projection is checked the same way. It is the first real
              economic content on the plane and 163 of its 165 specifications are
              uchiwake's own :representative rather than :authoritative, so a silent
              regeneration that dropped that label would turn inference into
              measurement."
