  {:id       :verify-source-path-pins
   :title    "cross-repo :source-path checkouts against the revision west.yml pins"
   :why      "A shadow-cljs build whose `:source-path` points at a sibling checkout compiles
              whatever revision that checkout happens to be at, which is not necessarily the
              one manifest/west.yml pins. The artifact is then unreproducible: nothing in it
              records which revision was compiled, and a rebuild on a machine whose checkout
              sits elsewhere produces different output from the same manifest.
              ⚠ **This detector has caught nothing, because nothing has ever run it on a
              schedule** -- ADR-2608196100 measured it as one of twelve verifiers with no
              runner and no twin. What justifies running it is not a past catch but a present
              measurement: 2026-08-19, 240 of 383 cross-repo source-paths resolve to a
              revision west.yml does not pin. The property it guards is violated at scale
              right now, and the registry's NEW/RESOLVED machinery is what turns that standing
              number into a signal when it moves.
              Adjacent and already registered: verify-shadow-source-paths asks whether a
              declared :source-path EXISTS. This asks whether the checkout behind it is the
              pinned revision. A build can pass the first and fail this one."
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" "{{repo}}:{{repo}}/scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-source-path-pins.cljs" "{{root}}"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\t"
   :interval-ms 21600000                 ; 6h
   :timeout-ms  600000                   ; 10m -- 37x the measured runtime, sized against
                                         ; load, not against the quiet number
   :writes   :none
   :measured "2026-08-19 on this machine, twice: 16s wall both times, at load 7.6 and 8.3.
              383 relative cross-repo :source-path entries across 31 shadow-cljs.edn files,
              240 findings, exit 1 -- it has no --report flag, and the tick does not need one
              because `:status` is never :ok on an exit code alone; the evidence regex has to
              match, and this detector prints SCANNED<TAB>383 before any finding.
              `{{root}}` is passed explicitly on purpose: the script's default root is a
              HARDCODED absolute path to this machine's checkout, so a tick running from a
              worktree would silently scan the wrong tree without it."}

  {:id       :verify-layer-deps
   :title    "deps.edn :local/root edges against the layer DAG in manifest/layers.edn"
   :why      "manifest/layers.edn declares a dependency DAG over the workspace's layers and
              this is the only thing that checks it. ADR-2607289600 records the state it is
              guarding against, measured: the layer plane is `定義のみ` -- west.yml has zero
              `layer-*` groups and gen-west-manifest.cljs does not read layers.edn -- so a
              violating :local/root edge is caught by NOTHING else in the pipeline. It has
              also already found real breakage: the Phase-1 dedup worklist
              (90-docs/2607171100-phase1-dedup-worklist.csv, row 210) records
              cloud-itonami-isic-855 with a :local/root one directory too high, credited to
              this script.
              ⚠ 2026-08-13 correction (ADR-2608132600): this line previously said the seven
              standing violations were `numbered directories re-created inside three app repos
              after layers.edn froze the list`. That was wrong, and it is the failure mode this
              registry's `:why` field is supposed to prevent -- a plausible story written from
              the finding text rather than from the repos. All seven directories were added
              between 2026-04-08 and 2026-06-26, BEFORE layers.edn froze the list on 2026-07-17
              (`git log --diff-filter=A`). They reappeared because layers.edn keys its exemption
              lists on WEST PATH, and three GitHub org-transfers and one rename moved the paths
              while the exemptions stayed: gftdcojp/app-aozora -> network-awai/app-aozora
              (gh id 1275051908), gftdcojp/club-shinshi -> network-awai/club-shinshi (1281275923),
              gftdcojp/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp -> gftdcojp/apps-gftdcojp (1136866292). Fixed in
              layers.edn; 7 -> 0. What this detector actually guards against is therefore two
              things, and only the first was written down: a violating :local/root edge, and an
              exemption list whose keys have drifted off the repos they exempt."
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" "{{repo}}:{{repo}}/scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-layer-deps.cljs" "--report" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\t"
   :interval-ms 21600000                 ; 6h
   :timeout-ms  900000                   ; 15m -- 7x the worst measured runtime
   :writes   :none
   :measured "2026-08-13 on this machine, twice, and the spread is the point. At load ~1
              (10 cores): 26.5s wall. At load 133: 2m06s wall for the same work, 10.1s of it
              user CPU -- it is waiting, not computing. Both runs: 4,415 repo directories
              under orgs/, 3,489 deps.edn parsed, 2,978 :local/root edges, 7 violations, all
              :internal-numbered-dir. exit 0 with --report (exit 1 without it). Reads only
              readdirSync/readFileSync plus one `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; no network,
              no writes. The 15m timeout is sized against the CONTENDED number, because this
