  {:id       :verify-tsukuru-factory-plane
   :title    "tsukuru's three factory datasets staying partitioned by CONSENT, not by realism"
   :why      "The three datasets differ by what each company agreed to -- research references
              with no consent, example seeds, and R0 worked examples -- and every way that
              distinction breaks is silent: a tag collapses, rows drop, a did:web leaks into
              the unconsented set, and Datalog keeps answering. The largest possible lie here
              is an un-onboarded company appearing as registered. It is also the detector
              that most recently WAS the failure it guards against: until 2026-08-13 an empty
              plane query made it skip all three checks and exit 0, the same shape as the five
              retired security-gate-* scripts, inside the verifier itself (ADR-2608130600).
              Its only scheduled caller is scripts/tsukuru-maturity-tick.cljs, driven by
              cloud.itonami.bot.tsukuru-maturity-tick -- one of the five plists ADR-2608124800 found
              was never installed. Registering it here gives it a home WITHOUT installing
              that plist, which also launches an autonomous model loop that commits and
              pushes; the ADR is explicit that those are different decisions."
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" "{{repo}}:{{repo}}/scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-tsukuru-factory-plane.cljs" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\t"
   :interval-ms 86400000                 ; 24h -- see :measured
   :timeout-ms  5400000                  ; 90m -- 4.9x the worst measured runtime
   :writes   :none
   :measured "2026-08-13 on this machine, twice. Standalone at load 157-187 on 10 cores:
              18m21s wall, of which 1093.4s is the single plane load + 3 queries, 256s user
              CPU. Through the tick itself at load ~110-157: 822s (13m42s), exit 0,
              scanned=2221, 0 findings -- so the timeout is 6.6x the tick measurement and
              4.9x the worst standalone one. exit 0, 0 findings,
              SCANNED 2,221 factory entities (candidates 2,119 / registry-seed 99 / seed 3,
              each above its floor; 3 datasets disjoint; 0 did:web in candidates; 0
              fabricated :company/lei). The script's own header records ~295s on a quiet
              host, so the load term dominates by 3.7x -- that spread is why it says to
              re-measure on the host before scheduling it, and why the timeout is sized on
              the LOADED number. 24h rather than 6h for the same reason
              verify-require-graph is: 256s of CPU four times a day on a machine already at
              load 157 is a real cost, and a consent-tier partition changes on human
              timescales. It reads EDN files and spawns exactly one child,
              `nbb manifest/edn-query.cljs q*`, which has no write call anywhere; no
              network, no writes."}

  {:id       :verify-namespace-collisions
   :title    "namespaces two repositories both ship"
   :why      "ADR-2608131700, 2026-08-13: two repos shipping one namespace means a build
              silently gets whichever the classpath reaches first, and the loser's code
              is dead while still looking live. Measured on this machine that day:
              `authentication.adapters.external-factors` does not compile at all on
              cloud-itonami/local-itonami's real classpath -- `No such var:
              oidc/verify-once` -- because org-openid-oidc's `oidc.core` sits ahead of
              kotoba-lang/oidc's and the two share no names. Nothing reported it. The
              same run found `kotoba.lang.package-registry` shipped by two repos with
              ten shared names and divergent bodies, one of which drops the
              :dep/definition-cids that stops a republish swapping a definition body.
              It cannot be a fleet gate: a gate is shipped only the target repo's own
              tree, and this question is about two trees at once."
   :argv     ["nbb" "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-namespace-collisions.cljs" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\t"
   :interval-ms 86400000                 ; 24h -- as expensive as verify-require-graph
   :timeout-ms  3600000                  ; 60m -- 2.6x the slowest measured run
   :writes   :none
   :measured "2026-08-13 on this machine, twice: 22.8m and 14.1m wall for the same corpus
              (the spread is other agents on this machine, not the corpus), 4045
              checked-out repos / 5438 source trees / 16406 file paths. 9 fail findings
              (co-classpath divergent) and 10 warn (EXTENSION-SHADOWED with no closure
              holding both). No --all: the 253 divergent-but-unreachable and 1544
              identical namespaces are scaffold families and would be 1500 standing
              lines. --findings was proved additive on a 3-repo fixture: output
