              and SCANNED lines are removed; --check still exits 1 either way."}

  {:id       :verify-appview-facade
   :title    "migrated appviews whose deployed handler is not the file a reader opens"
   :why      "2026-08-15, found while writing an operator quickstart for
              cloud-itonami/port and then asking whether it was one repo's quirk.
              It was not. Across all 329 appview repos in cloud-itonami and
              etzhayyim carrying a wrangler.jsonc: 175 deploy the SvelteKit build,
              147 ship an appview/*/src/app.ts facade, and 89 serve /health in
              that facade and in NO deployed route -- so 89 services document a
              health endpoint that hits the SvelteKit 404 in production, which is
              worse than having none because the source says 200. A further 58
              have request validation only in the undeployed file: the facade
              answers 400 InvalidJson while the deployed route does
              `.catch(() => ({}))` and calls the tool with EMPTY ARGUMENTS. Both
