              so. This is the same shape as the kotobase.net funnel that was fixed and
              then silently rolled back eleven minutes later by an older checkout
              (root ADR-2607285000): deploy has no fast-forward check, so last writer wins
              and being on main is not being served.
              It measures two separate things and does not merge them: whether the
              repository log verifies cryptographically (asked by running cloud-itonami's
              own bin/didwebvh.cljs verify in that checkout -- three of did:webvh's rules
              produce plausible, stable, wrong values when reimplemented, so a second
              implementation here would be one that gets fixed alone), and whether the
              live host serves those exact bytes.
              Cannot be a fleet gate: it needs orgs/network-awai/cloud-itonami AND six
              west siblings on the classpath, and no single shipped tree holds them."
   :argv     ["nbb" "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-itonami-did-webvh.cljs"
              "--root" "{{root}}" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
