  {:id       :verify-spec-var-claims
   :title    "spec files that name a var, checked against the branch other people get"
   :why      "2026-08-20: `kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang/lang/*.edn` names implementations by
              qualified symbol next to `:status :implemented`, and nothing resolved those
              names. Resolving them in the WORKING TREE and on the DEFAULT BRANCH gives
              different answers, and no output distinguished the two. Measured: 13 claims,
              12 resolve on disk, 10 on a default branch. The gap is
              `kotoba.value.codec/value-cid` and `verify-value-cid`, which exist only as an
              uncommitted 27-line addition in one shared checkout -- another session's
              in-flight work -- while value-codec.edn declares both `:implemented` under
              `:kotoba.lang.value-codec/logical-address`. A person checking locally sees
              them resolve; a fresh clone does not have them. A third,
              `kotoba.release-evidence/v2`, sits in a checkout 197 commits behind whose
              namespace is not on that repo's main at all. Dirty checkouts and stale
              checkouts produce the identical symptom: a name that resolves for you and
              for nobody else."
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" "{{repo}}:{{repo}}/scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-spec-var-claims.cljs" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\tclaim"
   :interval-ms 21600000                 ; 6h -- landing a var is a human act
   :timeout-ms  120000                   ; 2m -- 34x the measured run
   :writes   :none
   :measured "2026-08-20 on this machine: 5s wall, 13 claims, 9 findings, exit 1.
              Two defects were found by USING it, both of the class it reports:
                specs were read from the working tree while implementations were read
                from the ref -- the asymmetry it exists to catch, in its own input. Specs
                now come from the ref, and a local file that differs is reported, with
                `git status` asked whether it is MODIFIED or merely BEHIND rather than
                asserted: six differed and only one was a local edit; the other five were
                a checkout 52 commits behind.
                execSync`s default 1 MiB maxBuffer THROWS rather than truncating, and this
                helper turned that into nil, which every caller reads as absent. Two 2.25 MB
                spec files were reported `unreadable`; the same path runs over
                implementation files, where a large namespace would have produced a silent
                var-missing for every var in it. Raised to 64 MiB.
              A transient run returned exit 2 while another session held git in the same
              repo. That is the design working, not a flake to paper over: an unanswerable
              run must not report clean. Three consecutive runs after it: exit 1, 9 findings.
              2026-08-21: it went green on its own subject. The two working-tree-only
              findings were kotoba.value.codec/value-cid and verify-value-cid; landing them
              (io-ipld d25259e4) took the count from 10/13 to 12/13 with zero working-tree-only
              -- a red-to-green transition on the real target, not a synthetic one.
              The last standing finding was then this detector's OWN false positive:
              :evidence-schema \"kotoba.release-evidence/v2\" is a schema VERSION, the same
              kind of thing as :codec-id \"kotoba.value.v1\", and neither namespace surviving
              that one's split defines a v2. Key selection is now an ALLOWLIST rather than a
              denylist: a denylist needs a new entry per such key and until it gets one the
              report is wrong in the direction that costs most, a finding nobody can act on
              sitting next to findings they must. An allowlist is wrong the other way -- it
              stays quiet about a key it does not know -- so SKIPPED reports how often that
              happened and names the keys, and the evidence regex does not depend on it.
              Now 12/12, exit 0, SKIPPED 1 (:evidence-schema). Still discriminates: putting
              :evidence-schema back into the allowlist returns exit 1 with that finding.
              
              Only `git show`/`cat-file`/`remote` against already checked-out repos and
              fs reads; no network.
              Three states produced deliberately before registering:
                as-is                                   -> exit 1, 3 findings
                spec dir pointed at a path that is absent -> exit 2, SCANNED 0, refuses
                                                             (`Absence of claims is not
                                                              absence of drift`)
                dependency coordinates left un-excluded  -> exit 1, 4 findings, the extra
                                                             one being io.github.kotoba-lang/io-ipld
              The middle state is the point: a spec dir that is not checked out must not
              read as a clean spec dir, and 2 is neither 0 nor 1 so it cannot be mistaken
              for either. The third is why the coordinate exclusion exists rather than
              being left as noise a reader learns to skip.
              Known blind spot, stated in the finding text rather than hidden: namespaces
              are LOCATED by the working tree and only then verified against the ref, so a
              namespace present on a repo's main but missing from a stale checkout reports
              as `ns-missing` -- indistinguishable from one that exists nowhere. Locating
              by ref would mean an `ls-tree` per repository, roughly 4,400 of them, every
              run. It under-reports; it does not pass something bad.
              Do not rewrite any check here as a shell grep: `grep` on this machine is
              ugrep, which reads `(` as a group opener, so `grep \"^(ns foo.bar\"` matches
              nothing and reports every namespace absent. The first draft of this
              measurement concluded all four claims were missing for exactly that reason."}

  {:id       :verify-west-registration-gap
   :title    "repos other checkouts depend on that west does not carry"
   :why      "west 未登録の repo は、その repo を :local/root や :paths \"../…\" で参照して
              いる checkout を fresh clone / CI 上で壊す。ADR-2607173200 の実例:
              kotoba-lang/crm は GitHub に push 済み・west 未登録で、cloud-itonami-isic-5820
              / -6201 / -6202 の deps.edn が指していた。手元では解決するので誰も気づかない。
              この検査は 2026-08-23 まで **人が『cleanup』と打った時にしか走らなかった** ——
              skill git-cleanup-conflict の minimum workflow の step 1 に入っているだけで、
              打たれない限り登録漏れは何日でも積める。これを常設の測定にする。
              報告するのは **消費者の checkout が pin と一致している辺だけ**（audit の
              :live）。古い木で読んだ宣言は :stale-tree として exit 2 側に送られる ——
              2026-08-20 に、195 commit 遅れた checkout が main で既に直っていた宣言を
              報告し、その修正を書いて push するまで上流を読まなかった実例がある。
              **gh は呼ばない**（レジストリの gh class 規約）。そのため :true-orphan-git
              （誰もまだ依存していない未登録 repo）は finding にせず、CENSUS 行で
              『判定していない候補が N 件』とだけ言う —— gh 無しでは改名残骸と区別できず、
              実測 2026-08-23 では候補 43 件が 43 件とも改名残骸だった。そちらは
              nbb scripts/west-orphan-audit.cljs --all（gh 有り）と
              nbb scripts/west-triple-sync.cljs plan --scope orphans で人が見る。"
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" "{{repo}}:{{repo}}/scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/west-orphan-audit.cljs" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\tproject deps.edn read for :local/root"
   :interval-ms 21600000                 ; 6h -- 登録漏れは人が repo を着地させた時に生まれる
   :timeout-ms  600000                   ; 10m -- 実測 32s の 19x。この機械は load 100 まで振れる
   :writes   :none
   :measured "2026-08-23 on this machine, twice at load 25.8: 32.18s と 26.41s、出力同一、
              exit 0。SCANNED 4433 local orgs projects / 3676 deps.edn (:local/root) /
              3802 deps.edn (:paths)、CENSUS local-root-decls=3218 paths-decls=75
              west-paths=4225 unadjudicated-true-orphan-candidates=43。
              gh を 1 度も呼ばないことを PATH 上の spy で確認済み（呼び出しログ 0 行）。
              landing 前に 4 方向を実際に出した（合成 tree、orgs/acme/{consumer,lib-registered,lib-orphan}）:
                clean                                        -> exit 0、FINDING 0
                consumer が未登録 project を :local/root で参照 -> exit 1、FINDING 2
                                                                 （local-root: と rel-path: の両方）
                consumer の checkout が pin と不一致            -> exit 2、UNJUDGED 2、FINDING 0
                orgs/ の無い木（この repo の worktree）から実行  -> exit 3、SCANNED 0、CANNOT ANSWER
              最後の 1 つがこの entry の床である。orgs/ を持たない木では走査が 0 件で
              完走し、旧実装は『壊れた辺 0 件』= exit 0 を返した —— 『見ていない』が
              『無い』として記録される形（ADR-2608136000 の問 1/問 2）。
              現在の tree では finding 0 件で、それは blocking が実際に 0 だからである
              （2026-08-23 の全件測定: local-root-broken 0 / relative-paths-broken 0）。
              つまりこの detector は landing 時点で緑であり、**赤も実際に出せることを
