  {:id       :verify-actor-did-keys
   :title    "a key in a DID document outside the enumerated actor set"
   :why      "2026-09-01: etzhayyim.com resolves /actor/<handle>/did.json for ANY
              handle -- `definitely-not-an-actor-9x7q` returns 200 with a
              well-formed document -- and that is deliberate. Its own
              /.well-known/actors.json enumerates 104 named actors and then counts
              42,659 more as `society-scale keyless mirror-actors`, each namespace
              marked `keyless observational mirror -- NOT the entity itself (no
              impersonation, G1)`.

              The safety of that open namespace rests on one property: a document
              with no verification method cannot sign, so a mirror cannot speak as
              the thing it mirrors. Put a key in one and the mirror becomes an
              impersonator, and nothing about the URL changes to say so.

              This was nearly broken from the outside on the day it was written.
              Making the actor DID plane usable for agent authentication means
              putting keys in documents, and the obvious way to do it -- key the
              actors -- is right only for the enumerated ones. `tomoshibi`, the
              one keyed document today, is enumerated; that was the pattern, and
              nothing enforced it."
   :argv     ["nbb" "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-actor-did-keys.cljs" "--findings" "{{root}}"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*"
