  {:id       :verify-declared-dependencies
   :title    "src requires namespaces its own deps.edn does not account for"
   :why      "A require is resolved by the classpath, and in this workspace the classpath is
              assembled four ways -- `clojure -M:test`, a hand-written --classpath in
              bin/run_tests.cljs, shadow-cljs reading :deps, and a sibling checkout that
              happens to sit next door under orgs/. Three of the four put a dependency on the
              classpath whether or not deps.edn names it, so an undeclared require resolves
              for everyone who already has the dependency and for nobody else. The first
              person it does not resolve for is always a new consumer, part-way through its
              first run.
              Measured twice on 2026-09-06 in one session. (1) kotobase-protocol-core's
              deps.edn said `src has no dependencies at all ... verified by grep at the
              2026-08-05 split`; src/kotobase/protocols/blocks.cljc arrived AFTER that split
              and requires kotobase.store, so three surface repos needed the whole kotobase
              repository on the classpath with nothing declaring it and a fourth found out as
              `Could not find namespace: kotobase.store`. (2) net-kotobase/ipfs pinned io-ipld
              twelve commits behind the namespace a new file needed -- the same shape one
              layer down, where the coordinate is declared and the revision it names does not
