  {:id       :verify-lint-structural-warnings
   :title    "clj-kondo structural warnings: an if with no else, a when with no body"
   :why      "Every registered repository here carries the same lint alias -- clj-kondo
              2024.11.14, `--lint src test --fail-level error`. Measured 2026-09-06: 3,122 of
              the 4,331 paths manifest/west.yml pins declare it. NOTHING RUNS IT. GitHub
              Actions was retired fleet-wide (ADR-2607300900) and the 301 entries in
              scripts/fleet-ci/gates.edn contain no clj-kondo gate -- the one entry NAMED
              `lint` is nbb-cross-runtime-lint, which exercises the `lint` library on a second
              runtime and never invokes a linter.
              ADR-2607091500 (accepted, 2026-07-09) fixed that alias shape AND declared lint
              `CI の必須ジョブ` -- a required CI job. The later ADR retired the thing that ran
              it, and the enforcement clause was never re-homed. The alias has been inert ever
              since: present in three thousand deps.edn files, run in none.
              `--fail-level error` is the second half of the defect. Both ids below are
              :warning by default, so even on the day the alias last ran, every one of these
              exited 0. Only a mechanism that treats them as FINDINGS sees them.
              missing-else-branch, 9 sites in 6 files. Two had already been diagnosed by hand,
              at cost: network-awai/local-murakumo src/local_murakumo/worker.cljs:1546 lost its
              else, cljs compiled it as a `when`, and every non-streaming /v1/messages resolved
              to nil -- which the live Worker answered as 500 RangeError (fixed by hand
              2026-09-01 in d7225b7, while clj-kondo had been able to print `Missing else
              branch.` at it the whole time; it is absent from the sweep, which is the fix
              showing up). kotoba-lang/ayatori src/ayatori/remote.cljc:457 cost TWO
              discoveries and two fetches where none costs one, and killed the Node process on a
              rejecting source. RESOLVED 2026-09-06. The defect was real -- the if-not opened at
              457:37 and CLOSED at 469:89 with one child form, so the (try ...) on line 470 was
              its sibling, not its else -- but the repository's main had ALREADY been fixed
              (b539060, merged baceead7) and the west pin was ALREADY at that merge. Only the
              shared CHECKOUT lagged, at 408938c, and this detector reads the checkout; the
              fetch the first sweep recorded as refused in fact succeeds. `west update --fetch
              smart ayatori` cleared it and the site went with it.
              So checkout, west pin and main being three different things (ADR-2608136800) cuts
              BOTH ways here: a stale checkout makes this detector report a site that no longer
              exists in anything that ships -- a FALSE POSITIVE, the mirror of the silence the
              rest of this entry is about. A finding means `the tree on disk carries it`; check
              `git -C <path> rev-parse HEAD` against the pin before acting on one.
              The other four -- cloud-itonami-isic-3520, cloud-itonami-isic-853,
              network-awai/cloud-itonami and kototama-component -- had never been named anywhere
              before this ran, and neither had the sixth file the count includes without the
              prose naming it, kotoba-lang/ooyake
              src/ooyake/cells/world_model/state_machine.cljc:65.
              missing-body-in-when, 1 site, and it earns its place on evidence not symmetry:
              kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang test/kotoba/cli_test.cljc:116 is
              `(when (pos? ...) #?(:clj (System/exit 1)))`, and under :cljs the reader
              conditional yields nothing, so A FAILING SUITE DOES NOT EXIT NON-ZERO.
              SCOPED NARROWLY ON PURPOSE, and the price is visible in the run's own output: the
              sweep saw 20,325 clj-kondo findings of every kind and reported 10. unused-binding
              alone is 2,992 sites across 1,611 repos; unused-referred-var, unused-namespace,
              redundant-do, misplaced-docstring and single-logical-operand are this codebase's
              idiom or are cosmetic. A gate that lands red against thousands of sites is not a
              gate, and the 10 would be inside it.
              THIS DOES NOT RE-HOME ADR-2607091500's CLAUSE. It covers two ids of it. Every
              repository whose own --fail-level error alias would already be red if anything
              ran it is still unaddressed by this or by anything else; the error-level share of
              those 20,325 was not separated out, and stating it would be a number this entry
              did not measure.
              Unlike most entries here it COULD be a fleet gate for the per-repo half --
              clj-kondo needs only the target repository's tree. It is here because the
              question is fleet-wide (9 sites across 4,331 paths, four of them in repositories
              nobody would have thought to add a gate to), and because no node declares
              clj-kondo while the alias's own `clojure -M:lint` needs :jvm, which 2 of the 8
              nodes have."
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" ".:scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-lint-structural-warnings.cljs" "--findings"
              "--scan-root" "{{root}}"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*"
   :writes   :none
   :interval-ms 86400000                 ; 24h -- source moves in days and the sweep is long
   :timeout-ms  3600000                  ; 60m -- 3.5x the measured run, on a loaded machine
   :measured "2026-09-06 on this machine. Full sweep: 1020s wall, load average 17.4 rising to
              26.4 across the run -- the load is recorded beside the number because this
              workstation runs many concurrent agent sessions and most of that wall time is
              theirs. SCANNED 33,269 source files across the 3,766 repos that have a src/ or
              test/, of 4,331 registered paths; 539 had neither and are out of scope; 9 files
              did not parse. Exit 2: 7 findings (10 sites) and 35 things that could not be
              linted -- 26 registered paths with no checkout and 9 unparseable files. Exit 2
              rather than 1 is the honest state: until those 35 can be read, `neither id occurs
              anywhere` is not a claim this detector is entitled to make.
              NOT `accepted`: an acceptance names a finding key, and every unmeasured row here
              is a thing the run genuinely did not measure, not a finding understood and
              deferred. Recording them as accepted would put an exit-2 reason inside the class
              the registry reserves for findings.
              Both directions were watched on the real tree before landing, not asserted.
              FINDS IT: --repo kototama-component --repo ooyake exits 1 with exactly the two
              sites, at 528:3 and 65:9. GOES CLEAN: --repo prolly-tree exits 0 having linted 12
              files with 0 clj-kondo findings of any kind. REFUSES: --repo property exits 2 on
              src/kotoba/property/query.clj, which clj-kondo cannot parse, while still linting
              the other 78 files in that repository -- an unreadable file does not blind the
              repo around it.
              `--selftest` builds its own trees and shows eleven things change colour,
              including three that are easy to get silently wrong: a repository whose own
              .clj-kondo/config.edn sets both ids to :level :off is STILL reported (without the
              forced --config, clj-kondo prints `:findings []` there and this would report
              clean having measured nothing); linting leaves no .clj-kondo/.cache behind, which
              is what `--cache false` buys and what makes :writes :none true -- 24 registered
              repositories already have a .clj-kondo directory, and clj-kondo writes a cache
              into exactly those; and the excluded ids stay quiet on a file deliberately full
              of them.
              The clj-kondo BINARY on PATH is used, not `clojure -M:lint`: same pinned version
              (checked at startup, and a mismatch or an absent binary is exit 2 before any
              sweep), ~10ms startup against the JVM's seconds, and no contention for the build
              lock. Skipping the classpath cache cannot change these two answers -- a populated
              cache moves unresolved-namespace and unresolved-symbol counts, which need to know
              what another namespace defines, while missing-else-branch and missing-body-in-when
              are decided from the arity of one form and see nothing outside the file.
              It reads WORKING TREES, like verify-declared-dependencies and for the same
              reason. The ayatori finding is what that costs and what it buys: the fix is said
              to exist and is not in the checkout, so the defect is really there for anyone
              running this code. Check the repository's main before acting on a finding."}
  {:id       :verify-pages-freshness
   :title    "公開ページが、その repo の default branch より何 commit 前に建てられたものか"
   :why      "2026-09-08、kotoba-lang/kami-app-suji の公開ページは HTTP 200 を返して
              普通に開けたが、中身は 2 日前の build で、その間に着地した波 —— 可視量
              50 → 86、結合解の報告、動員されていない 11 筋が『軽く負荷』と塗られていた
              欠陥の修正 —— は 1 つも live に無かった。**古いページも 200 を返す。**
              CLAUDE.md の single-page app 規則は『見られることは規則の半分』と書いて
              いて、これはその裏面 —— document は出ているが中身が古い。ソースからは
              見えず、開いても見えない。
              同じ日、その publish を行うスクリプトの docstring と過去の publish commit
              すべてが『Actions が repo 全体で無効だから前回の artifact は失敗せずに
              古くなった』と書いていたが、GitHub に訊くと {\"enabled\":true} だった ——
              **理由の側が偽になっていた**ので、理由を読まずに時刻と commit を数える。
              ⚠ **その 52 という数は、この検出器自身の枠組みの誤りだった**（2026-09-08、
              同日に訂正）。root だけを引いて 404 なら『人が開けない』と報告していたが、
              調べると 52 のうち少なくとも 48 は **site は配信していて root に index が
              無いだけ**だった —— cargo は `/` が 404 で `/.well-known/did.json` が 200、
              isco-1111 は `/` が 404 で `/samples/operator-console.html` が 200。
              いまは root が 404 のとき **source ディレクトリの実ファイルを 1 本引いて**、
              『何も配信していない』と『入口が無い』を分ける。
              全件（8 org / Pages 有効 524 repo）で測ると: **URL が 200 を返さない 52**、
              build 記録あり 496、build より後に commit が在る 444（うち status が
              built でないもの 6 —— building 5 / errored 1）、遅れの中央値 5・最大 51。
              444 を 1 件ずつ finding にすると使われなくなるので、**個別 finding は
              境界が導出できる 2 つ**（開けない / build が完了していない）に限り、
              残りは母数と最悪値を持つ 1 行の集計 finding にした。列挙しないことと
              数えていないことは別である。"
   :argv ["nbb" "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-pages-freshness.cljs" "--findings"]
   :cwd :root
   :findings :protocol
   :writes   :none
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*"
   :timeout-ms 2700000
   :interval-ms 86400000
   :measured "GitHub の credential を要するのでノードでは引けない —— fleet gate に
              できない理由は orgs/ を読むことではなく、鍵を持たないことのほう
              （不変条件3）。1 repo につき /pages・pages/builds/latest・commits?since の
              3 リクエストと、**URL への実 GET 1 本**。API だけでは足りないことは実測で
              決まった: build_type が workflow の repo は /pages の status が null で
              build 記録が 404 を返すが URL は 200 を配っており（kotoba, svgraph）、
              API の沈黙を『建っていない』と読むと嘘になる。
              数えているのは『build より後に着地した commit の本数』だけで、これは
              サイトが間違っているという主張ではない —— README だけを直した commit なら
              site は正しいまま。だから severity は warn、閾値は無い（> 0 だけが導出
              できる境界で、それ以外は発明した定数になる）。commits の件数は 1 ページ
              ぶんしか引かないので 100 で頭打ちになり、そのときは `100+` と印字する。
              両方向を見た: org を引けなければ REFUSED で exit 2（実測、実在しない org
              名で確認）。serving? を常に真にすると ① が空になり、commits-since を 0 に
              固定すると ② が空になる —— どちらも復元は sha256 一致。"}
  {:id       :verify-capability-provider-status
